  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Hey,\n\nI don't think I need to tell you that VRchat is an important part of a lot of your users' lives. I hope you know that.\n\nI was not able to log in due to work for a while, but I cannot put into words how much I was looking forward to meeting my friends and loved ones in VR and spending time with them for the first time this year. Today, when I finally found some time to do that, I was greeted by the \"Does not work on virtual machine\" message. \n\nThe same issue in december luckily went past me, I did not even notice, but when I saw that message, my heart dropped.\n\nI use a shadow PC as I simply cannot afford the huge investment of buying a gaming PC capable of running VRchat in decent quality in VR. This setup has worked fine for the most part.\n\nShadow PC support says that the issue is with you, or the anticheat (EAC) on your end. You say in another thread (which you closed) that the issue is with Shadow PC. In this thread multiple people cite ShadowPC support, which says that they have contacted you trying to find a solution. \n\nAre there any updates? What is going on?\n\nIt must be possible to reach out to EAC and figure out a solution. \n\nPlease don't just merge this into the other thread.\n\nAll the best",
